Fixes bugs of the latest release (2.1.0), mostly to make `stringifyAsync`
behave like `JSON.stringify`.

`utils/index-of-generator.js`:

1. `chunk` is assigned without being declared.
   In the original CommonJS code, this silently creates a global variable.
   Our bundle is strict-mode ESM, where it throws a `ReferenceError` instead,
   so `jsonParseAsync` rejected every input.
   Backported from an unreleased upstream commit:
   https://github.com/ibmruntimes/yieldable-json/commit/be95a02e16006111393a36886e22da5e7b1b2cb2

`index.js`:

2. A numeric `space` is read from the next argument.
   Our `jsonStringifyAsync` relies on this fix: check it before dropping this part.
3. `space` isn't limited like in `JSON.stringify`: strings are cut to 9
   characters instead of 10 (or not cut at all), and numbers are rounded
   instead of truncated.

`yieldable-stringify.js`:

4. With `space`, nested objects and arrays all get the same single level of
   indentation.
   Reported, but not fixed upstream:
   https://github.com/ibmruntimes/yieldable-json/issues/32
5. Values with `toJSON` (like `Date`) get extra whitespace with `space`, and
   the replacer gets them before `toJSON` is called.
   The upstream commit above fixes the whitespace, but then calls the replacer
   a second time, with an empty key.
   Here, `toJSON` is called before the replacer instead, like in `JSON.stringify`.
6. `intensity` is ignored: `1` is always used.
7. Array indexes are passed to the replacer and `toJSON` as numbers.
8. Numbers in a replacer array are ignored, and duplicates aren't skipped.
9. Control characters aren't escaped, so the output isn't valid JSON.
   Reported, with an open PR that is backported here:
   https://github.com/ibmruntimes/yieldable-json/issues/56
   https://github.com/ibmruntimes/yieldable-json/pull/57
   That PR alone breaks strings over 100 000 characters when their last chunk
   contains a control character, so that is fixed too.
10. All calls share the same state, so concurrent calls can mix up strings over
    100 000 characters, or fail with "Circular Structure Detected".
    Reported in https://github.com/ibmruntimes/yieldable-json/issues/8, which is
    closed, but the state is still shared.

Drop each part once a release includes its fix.

